# What is in the repository but must NOT be readable at the domain.
#
# A root-directory deploy publishes every file it can see. These are kept in
# git deliberately and are still internal: the build tooling, the session
# handoff notes, the simulated-traffic peer review that documents the site's
# own defects, and a spec carrying local filesystem paths.
#
# gitignore syntax. Anything not listed here IS public, so add to this file
# before adding a new non-public directory to the repository.

.git
.gitignore
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc

# Internal notes and tooling
docs
scripts
.handoffs
.superpowers
README.md

# Development leftovers
home.png
*.log
